    <string name="cs_title">Share rounded summaries with the cloud?</string>
    <string name="cs_sent_h">WHAT IS SENT (to DeepInfra, only when you tap Ask):</string>
    <string name="cs_sent_b">• Total money rounded to 2 significant figures\n• Cash / bills / earning as whole percentages\n• Lending lines: protocol, asset symbol, share, yearly rate\n• Bills grouped by due window: count and rounded total\n• Last 30 days of spending by fixed category: rounded totals\n• Days of cash left, and the question you type</string>
    <string name="cs_never_h">WHAT IS NEVER SENT:</string>
    <string name="cs_never_b">• Private keys, seed phrases, your API key\n• Wallet or contract addresses, transaction hashes\n• Invoice IDs, names of who you pay, memos, category labels\n• Exact balances or amounts, exact dates\n• Anything the privacy filter does not recognise</string>
    <string name="cs_foot">The cloud model is read-only: it returns advice text only and cannot move or approve money. You can see every message sent in the activity list, and turn this off at any time. DeepInfra says it does not store prompts or outputs; Google and Anthropic models are blocked because those providers do.</string>
    <string name="cs_accept">I understand, turn on</string>
